  {
   "id": 543951,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Recall that the bridges of Konigsberg can be represented as a multigraph as shown in the figure. We have seen that no route through Konigsberg passes over each bridge exactly once and returns to the starting point. Is there a route that passes over each bridge exactly once but does not begin and end at the same point? Explain your reasoning.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b364ef0c16a7daff.png\" alt=\"A graph of Konigsberg Bridges has four vertices. The vertices are connected with edges forming two right cones.\">\n",
